<content><![CDATA[<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>
<multiple-choice question="In two-point perspective, how many vanishing points sit on the horizon line?" single-option="" randomize="">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Two" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="One">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Three">
  <input type="checkbox" value="None">
</multiple-choice>
<true-false-question question="Orthographic views (front, side and top) are useful references for modeling to scale.">
  <input type="checkbox" value="True" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="False">
</true-false-question>
<self-check title="Think it through">
  <p slot="question">How does sketching a concept before modeling save time in 3D?</p>
  <p>Sketches let you explore shapes, proportions and silhouettes quickly, solve design problems before committing to geometry, and produce reference views to model from.</p>
</self-check>
